From db6487bb388f726010b35d0b6d0707b6f6b462fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guideboard Labs <contact@guideboardlabs.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:02:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ggml: add fused mHC residual-stream routing ops

Two nodes replace roughly a hundred per router: ggml_mhc_route folds the
streams, normalises, projects the eight router logits and runs the sinkhorn
passes; ggml_mhc_merge mixes the 2x2 matrix and adds the sublayer output.

Implemented for the CPU backend and as Vulkan compute shaders, so a graph
that uses them stays on device instead of being cut once per router.
